{
  "id": "T-PUPPETFLIPS",
  "title": "H-PUPPETSTUTTER-1, two players: the watcher's customer copies stop and start walking as often as the real customers do. The client's fast-food shop at normal speed, the client simulating (owner, enters first) and the host watching; 60 s of IsMoving true->false counts on both machines via `puppetflips`. NO save.",
  "preconditions": "Reporter fixture session fx-hq1 (day 44, MERGED - vars.keepMerger true). Dev build with H-PUPPETSTUTTER-1 (puppetflips / custstate / enterbuilding / exitbuilding / skipvote / skipstate, BAMP_DEV). The fixture loads at 17:38 with Client1 inside a building, so both step outside and take one consensus skip OUTDOORS to 10:45 the next morning (as T-HANDOFF1 does). The fast food at vars.shop is the CLIENT's (t-shopday-pick), so the client enters first and simulates it; the host follows and renders copies from the client's stream. ORACLE: watcher flips per minute (host, copies) within 1.5x of simulator flips per minute (client, natives sampled at each stream tick) - `puppetflips vs <n>` on the host computes the ratio. Before the fix the design expects watcher >> simulator (the chase slowed each copy to a stop between rows and late reliable rows stopped the walk).",
  "instances": 2,
  "vars": {
    "clientPid": "Client1",
    "hostPid": "melaus",
    "session": "fx-hq1",
    "keepMerger": true,
    "shop": "11 ba:street_tenthavenue"
  },
  "oracles_absent": [
    "\\[TickIso\\]",
    "\\[Guard\\]",
    "(?<!swallowed )NullReferenceException",
    "\\[Customers\\] (puppet tick|apply puppets|puppet spawn):",
    "ERR puppetflips"
  ],
  "oracles_report": [
    "\\[Customers\\] following ",
    "\\[Customers\\] simulator for ",
    "\\[Customers\\] puppet rig",
    "\\[TestDrive\\] puppetflips"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "host",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "join",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "hostload ${session}",
      "expect_result": "^OK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 4,
      "role": "both",
      "cmd": "mark TEST T-PUPPETFLIPS START",
      "expect_result": "OK MARK"
    },
    {
      "seq": 5,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 32,
      "note": "both worlds settle"
    },
    {
      "seq": 6,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "status",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "note": "settle poll (report-only): the HOST's own world can still be loading here (run T-HANDOFF2-20260926-213941 read settled=False at 39 s)"
    },
    {
      "seq": 7,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 20
    },
    {
      "seq": 8,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "status",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "note": "settle poll (report-only)"
    },
    {
      "seq": 9,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 20
    },
    {
      "seq": 10,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "status",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "note": "settle poll (report-only)"
    },
    {
      "seq": 11,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 18
    },
    {
      "seq": 12,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "status",
      "expect_result": "settled=True",
      "note": "ASSERT the host settled, bounded at ~90 s after the load (rigrun has no retry-until primitive, so the ladder always runs its full length)"
    },
    {
      "seq": 13,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "status",
      "expect_result": "settled=True"
    },
    {
      "seq": 14,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "exitbuilding",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "note": "fx-hq1 loads Client1 inside a building; report-only"
    },
    {
      "seq": 15,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "exitbuilding",
      "abort_on_fail": false
    },
    {
      "seq": 16,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 8
    },
    {
      "seq": 17,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skipvote 10:45",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal="
    },
    {
      "seq": 18,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "skipvote 10:45",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal=",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "expect_log": [
        {
          "role": "h",
          "regex": "\\[Rest\\] CONSENSUS \\(2/2\\)",
          "within_s": 60
        }
      ],
      "note": "the setup skip to the next trading morning, taken OUTDOORS"
    },
    {
      "seq": 19,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 40
    },
    {
      "seq": 20,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skipstate",
      "expect_result": "active=False"
    },
    {
      "seq": 21,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "skipvote off",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal=-"
    },
    {
      "seq": 22,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "skipvote off",
      "expect_result": "^OK skipvote goal=-"
    },
    {
      "seq": 23,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 5
    },
    {
      "seq": 24,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "enterbuilding ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK enterbuilding",
      "note": "the OWNER (client) enters first: he books the shop and simulates it"
    },
    {
      "seq": 25,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "enterbuilding ${shop}",
      "expect_result": "^OK enterbuilding",
      "note": "the host watches: copies driven by the client's stream"
    },
    {
      "seq": 26,
      "role": "c",
      "sleep_s": 6
    },
    {
      "seq": 27,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "custstate arm 3",
      "expect_result": "^OK custstate armed n=3 bldg='${shop}'",
      "abort_on_fail": false,
      "expect_log": [
        {
          "role": "c",
          "regex": "\\[Handoff\\] armed count reached: ([3-9]|[1-9][0-9]+) >= 3",
          "within_s": 180
        }
      ],
      "note": "THE PREMISE WAIT: the simulator's interior holds 3 live customers (an event, not a sleep)"
    },
    {
      "seq": 28,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "custstate",
      "expect_result": "^OK custstate bldg='${shop}' sim='${clientPid}' mode=native natives=[1-9]",
      "capture": {
        "cNat": "natives=(\\d+)"
      }
    },
    {
      "seq": 29,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "custstate",
      "expect_result": "^OK custstate bldg='${shop}' sim='${clientPid}' mode=follower natives=0 .*copies=[1-9]",
      "capture": {
        "hCopies": "copies=(\\d+)"
      },
      "note": "PREMISE: the host is a FOLLOWER holding copies"
    },
    {
      "seq": 30,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "puppetflips reset",
      "expect_result": "^OK puppetflips reset"
    },
    {
      "seq": 31,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "puppetflips reset",
      "expect_result": "^OK puppetflips reset"
    },
    {
      "seq": 32,
      "role": "h",
      "sleep_s": 60,
      "note": "THE WINDOW: 60 real seconds of normal-speed shopping"
    },
    {
      "seq": 33,
      "role": "c",
      "cmd": "puppetflips",
      "expect_result": "^OK puppetflips secs=[0-9.]+ sim=[1-9][0-9]* simPerMin=[0-9.]+ .*simMoving=[1-9]",
      "capture": {
        "simFlips": " sim=(\\d+)",
        "simPm": "simPerMin=([0-9.]+)",
        "simSamples": "simSamples=(\\d+)",
        "simMoving": "simMoving=(\\d+)",
        "cWatch": " watch=(\\d+)"
      },
      "note": "the SIMULATOR's natives: walk stops per minute, sampled at each stream tick (premise: somebody walked and stopped)"
    },
    {
      "seq": 34,
      "role": "h",
      "cmd": "puppetflips vs ${simPm}",
      "expect_result": "^OK puppetflips .* watch=[0-9]+ watchPerMin=[0-9.]+ .*follower=True .* ratio=[0-9.]+ within=True",
      "capture": {
        "watchFlips": " watch=(\\d+)",
        "watchPm": "watchPerMin=([0-9.]+)",
        "ratio": "ratio=([0-9.]+)",
        "watchMovingFrames": "watchMovingFrames=(\\d+)"
      },
      "note": "THE ASSERTION: the watcher's copies stop walking within 1.5x as often as the real customers (before the fix: many times more)"
    },
    {
      "seq": 35,
      "role": "both",
      "cmd": "mark TEST T-PUPPETFLIPS END",
      "expect_result": "OK MARK"
    }
  ]
}